📗
  🏥 The diagnostic app. Its routes report what the server saw and produce
  awkward responses on demand, so tests can check the engine from outside.

    /                      text "ok"
    /inspect[/:value]      GET POST PUT PATCH DELETE: one fact per line
    POST /bytes            the request body, byte for byte
    POST /json             the request body read as JSON and written back, or a 400 that says why it is not JSON
    /stream/:count         that many chunks, streamed; ?delay=ms waits before each later chunk
    /eight/:a/…/:h         its eight parameters, joined with commas
    /items                 puts eight items in the request's bag and reads them back
    /id                    the request's ID, as the handler sees it
    /own-id                an answer that brings an X-Request-Id of its own
    /status/:code          that status, with the body "body"
    /header?value=…        puts the value in an X-Echo response header
    /framing               sets the headers that only the server may set
    /stop                  asks the server to stop, then answers
    /slow/:ms              answers after that many milliseconds
    /raise/problem         raises a 404 problem with a message for a field
    /raise/plain           raises an error that carries no problem
    POST /raise/late       reads the body as JSON, then raises: a 422 if it was JSON
    /raise/again           catches what something it called raised, and raises it again
    /raise/status/:code    raises a problem with that status
    /kinds/new, /kinds/:id:int, /kinds/:name, /kinds/opt/:value?, /kinds/rest/*path
                           a route of each kind: the pattern that matched, and its parameters
    DELETE /kinds/new      the same, so that the path has two methods
    /only/:id:int          a route that nothing but an integer reaches
    /noted/:id:int         a route with the note stamp=yes
    /old/…                 answered as /kinds/…, by a layer that makes a request of its own and hands it on
    /go?to=…&status=…      redirects there, with that status when one is given
    /go/home?to=…          redirects there when it is a path on this site, and to / when it is not
    /cookie?name=…&value=…&also=…
                           sets that cookie when a name is given, and one more of the same value when also
                           names it; answers with the cookies it was sent, one name=value a line
    /cookie/drop?name=…    removes that cookie
    /tagged?body=…         the text, with a tag made from it; a request that brings the tag gets a 304
    /dated                 a body that was last changed on 6 November 1994, and says so
    /sized/:count:int?claim=…&piece=…
                           that many bytes, the digits 0 to 9 over and over, written in pieces (of 7 unless
                           piece says otherwise) as a body of known length, which is count unless claim lies
    /download?name=…       the text "file", as a download with that name
    /file?path=…           that file
    /file/lie?path=…&claim=…
                           a body that promises claim bytes of that file, whatever its size is: what a file
                           looks like that became shorter, or went away, after it was looked at
    /or/:id                what the accessors with a fallback give: the parameter as an integer and as text,
                           ?q, X-Thing, an item of the bag that is there and one that is not
    POST /bind/:id:int     binds an integer from the route, a text, an integer, a number, a choice and an
                           optional boolean from the body and an optional integer from the query: what it
                           read, or the binder's 400
